cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the article that
  introduces the protocol.
title: "treatment-identity: verify that the treatment an experiment declares is the one its data loader delivers"
abstract: >-
  Eight CPU treatment-delivery gates probe the loader output declared by an
  experiment, and a separate geometry gate checks evaluation integrity.
  Release 1.11.0 probes content scaling at five source shapes (16:9, 4:3,
  1:1, 3:4 and 9:16), tells the two axes of the scale fixture apart by
  waveform as well as by colour, and reads a fixed output shape as one policy
  item by item. Release 1.10.0 made two measurements general: the temporal index is read
  after a loader's fixed-size resize, and content scaling reports a rotation at
  any angle, measured from the two-dimensional spectrum, beside the scale of
  each axis. Release 1.9.0 extended the portability campaign from ten to
  sixteen loaders from fifteen projects and corrected the defects those loaders
  exposed; it carried the 2026-09-08 review corrections.
